messages:
maria: Quick sync — product/console wants new GPU metrics for Hosted + Dedicated pools. We need to lock metric names, labels, and dashboard layout. Primary signals: SM occupancy, SM memory (used/total), queue depth (per-slot + per-pool), and slot health. Who can own the ingest schema + prom mapping? @jonathan @lee

jonathan: I can own the ingest proto and prom mapping. One question — sampling cadence? 5s for realtime, or 15s to reduce churn?

lee: For perf-sensitive dashboards 5s is useful. For long-term rollups 30s is fine. We should emit both raw and an aggregated stream. Tagging: pool_type (hosted|dedicated), pool_id, region, model_family.

sarah: From console side we need per-customer aggregation and a toggle to switch hosted/dedicated views. Also want per-model SKU breakdown to show cost impact.

ankit: Add `batch_size` and `inflight_requests` labels — very helpful to correlate queue spikes. If possible expose `kv_cache_hit_ratio` and `allocator_fragmentation_ratio` per-GPU.

maria: Good call. Also define `slot_health` as a gauge (1 = healthy, 0 = degraded). For occupancy expose `sm_occupancy_percent` (0-100). For queue depth we should emit a gauge and a histogram (percentiles) so graphs + SLOs both possible.

jonathan: Proto sketch (very rough) ->
```proto
message GpuPoolSample {
  int64 ts = 1;
  string pool_id = 2;
  string pool_type = 3; // hosted|dedicated
  string region = 4;
  repeated GpuSmStats sm = 5;
}
message GpuSmStats {
  int32 sm_id = 1;
  float occupancy_percent = 2;
  uint64 memory_used_bytes = 3;
  uint64 memory_total_bytes = 4;
  uint32 queue_depth = 5;
  uint32 inflight_requests = 6;
  float kv_cache_hit_ratio = 7;
}
```

jonathan: Prometheus naming suggestion: `redwood_gpu_sm_occupancy_percent{pool_id, pool_type, region, model_family}`, `redwood_gpu_sm_memory_used_bytes`, `redwood_gpu_queue_depth`, `redwood_gpu_inflight_requests`, and histogram `redwood_gpu_queue_depth_bucket`.

lee: Agreed. For aggregation keys, use `pool_id` + `pool_type` + `region`. We also need a synthetic `pool_capacity_slots` gauge so headroom dashboards can compute available slots easily.

sarah: Dashboard layout idea: top row = cluster/pool headroom + overall CPU/GPU health, second row = per-SM occupancy heatmap (by pool), third row = top N queues and per-customer queue contribution, bottom = canary/rollout view with model pinned. Also add a small panel showing expected cost delta when switching quantization profiles.

ankit: Alerting rules proposal: Hosted: `queue_depth > 50 for 1m` -> P1 to paging oncall. Dedicated: alert when `queue_depth / reserved_slots > 0.9 for 2m` since thresholds vary by contract. Add runbook note: fallback to model-variant routing.

maria: UX/rollout notes — when we flip new metrics on, Console should show a banner: "metrics in pilot — values may be incomplete" and a canary toggle to opt-in tenant dashboards. Also ensure anonymized customer grouping for hosted by default.

telemetry-bot: Created ticket RINF-8943: "GPU telemetry onboarding - Hosted + Dedicated" assigned to @jonathan and @lee. Link: https://rdev/repo/infra/telemetry/issues/8943

jonathan: I'll push a draft proto + prom scrape adapter PR to git and attach a grafana dashboard JSON. ETA: EOD Friday. :thumbsup:

maria: Thanks — I'll schedule a 30m sync Wed to finalize owners and SLA thresholds.

lee: I'll start a grafana skeleton and share panels in the PR for quick review.

ankit: I'll work on alert runbook and oncall routing rules once the metrics names are final.

sarah: Noted — will prepare console patches (aggregation endpoints) after the proto lands.

maria: Perfect. If anyone has objections to the prom names or labels, flag them in the PR.
